--> Leaders in Array
-->An element is a leader if it is greater than or equal to all elements on its right.

Brute Force Approach:

package com.basics;
import java.util.LinkedList;
public class Main {
	public static boolean isLeader(int element, int ind, int [] arr){
        for(int i=ind; i<arr.length; i++){
            if(element < arr[i]){
                return false;
            }
        }
        return true;
    }

    public static void main(String args []) {
        LinkedList<Integer> list = new LinkedList<Integer>();
        int [] ar = {36,36, 15, 4, 30, 5, 2};
        for(int i=0; i<ar.length; i++){
            if(isLeader(ar[i], i+1, ar)){
                list.addFirst(ar[i]);
            }
        }
        for(int x : list) {
        	System.out.print(x + " ");
        }
    }
}

Time Complexity : O(n²)
